  "summary": "New preprints extend reproducible software for microbial genomics and amplicon data to species-level resolution and private deployment.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is accessible, reproducible computational tooling for microbial genomics and amplicon profiling. VPHYL converts Emu and EPI2ME wf-16s nanopore 16S abundance tables into phyloseq and BIOM objects. RADSuite pairs a curated 16S rRNA gene copy database with RADx to enable species-level microbiome identification. nf-core/pairgenomealign offers a scalable Nextflow pipeline using LAST for pairwise whole-genome alignment, and Sparrowhawk delivers private, in-browser microbial genomics via WebAssembly. Two items extend the theme to other settings: MAUDE-Py reimplements pooled CRISPR screen analysis in Python with faster runtime and near-identical results, and a Fusion transpiling study tests functional identity of SNHA code across nine languages. What is new is primarily at the tool level, namely workflow design, interoperability and privacy-preserving deployment, rather than new biological findings.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
